<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Forage</h1>
<p>Skill
Class: Ranger (guild level 3, up to 75%), Druid (guild level 6)
</p><p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>forage
</pre>
<p>You search the land around you for something to eat. It costs 20 
endurance, and you must be standing. Whatever you find is left on the 
ground at your feet, so pick it up. What you can find depends on the 
land:
</p>
<pre>field, hills      roots, tubers, berries, grubs, a bird egg
forest            all of those, and mushrooms, truffles, fruit and nuts
mountains         berries, grubs, a bird egg
desert            a lizard
swamp             newts, algae, kelp, fish, bullfrogs, snails, slugs
water             newts, algae, kelp, fish, bullfrogs
snow, slush       roots, tubers
city, indoors, ice   nothing at all
</pre>
<p>Your skill decides whether you find anything. Mountains and swamps are 
the easiest places to forage, hills and water a little harder, fields and 
forests harder still, and the desert and snow the hardest. Fail, and you 
find nothing, or only dirt.
</p><p>Beware: wild food is not always safe. Some of what you find is poisoned, 
mushrooms, slugs and snails most often, and eggs, nuts and truffles 
least.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
